---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Rosette from 'verdigris/astro/Rosette.astro';
---

<SiteLayout title="About" description="About the Verdigris design kit.">
  <!-- The live rosette, whole and in the theme's colors, beside the text from 768px. Hero takes
       only an image, so its markup is written out here, as on the home page. -->
  <header class="hero hero--split">
    <div class="hero-text">
      <h1 class="display">About</h1>
      <p class="lead hero-lead">
        I'm Danny Englander, and I designed Verdigris in collaboration with Claude Code. It starts from my Swiss
        Minimal kit, and adds Cormorant, copper and a little ornament.
      </p>
      <p class="lead hero-lead">
        Verdigris is a small design kit for type-led sites: one family, flat color, the scotch rule and
        ornament that earns its place, and <a class="link" href="/agents/">works well with AI agents</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="figure hero-figure">
      <Rosette />
      <figcaption>The home page rosette, drawn in the theme's colors.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </header>
  <article class="max-w-2xl pb-16 [&>p]:mb-5">
    <p>
      This page exists to check the type scale on running text. Body copy sits at 26px with a line height of
      1.55 (22px on phones), because Cormorant is small on its body. Headings rely on size alone, in the light weight; there are
      no colored headings and no boxes to prop them up.
    </p>
    <p>
      The palette is paper, ink and two metals. Cream paper, a green-black ink, a muted grey-green for secondary text,
      verdigris for the one thing that matters on a screen, and copper for labels and ornament. Small
      text in either metal uses a darker tone on the page so it still passes contrast.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each page of the menu has its own link. Write to us on the <a class="link" href="#contact">contact page</a>,
      or see the <a class="link" href="#features">features</a> and when each arrived.
    </p>
    <p>
      Code is the one place a second family appears. To start a site,
      install the <code>verdigris</code> package and import the kit from your
      global stylesheet; press <kbd>Tab</kbd> to see the focus ring.
    </p>
    <pre class="mb-5" tabindex="0"><code>@import "verdigris/tailwind.css";
/* site-only CSS below */</code></pre>
    <p>
      Terminal output and logs sit on a dark block, the same in both themes, with commands in bold and
      errors in the accent.
    </p>
    <pre class="pre--bar mb-5" tabindex="0"><code><span class="pre-cmd">$ npm run release -- --dry-run</span>
Tag v2026.10.21, notes from the Features list
<span class="pre-err">Stopped: main is behind origin/main. Pull first.</span></code></pre>
    <p class="small muted">
      Set in Cormorant, by Christian Thalmann, released under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
    </p>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
